          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-12548"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "A heap out-of-bounds read flaw was found in libsoup. When parsing multipart HTTP messages, an integer type mismatch between the caller and soup_headers_parse() can cause the length parameter to be incorrectly truncated, leading to a heap buffer over-read. A remote attacker could use this flaw to crash an application using libsoup or potentially disclose heap memory contents.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
